<main class="lp-page" id="crm-guide">
  <div class="lp-hero-shell"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <nav class="lp-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/resources/outbound-sales-library/">Outbound Sales Library</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">CRM for outbound sales</span></nav>
    <div class="lp-hero">
      <div><p class="lp-kicker">The CallTeam buying desk / 04</p><h1>7 best CRMs for <span>outbound sales<br>and cold calling.</span></h1><p class="lp-intro">Compare seven CRMs for calling and follow-up, including plan prices, extra costs and what to test during your trial.</p><div class="lp-actions"><a class="lp-button" href="#comparison">Compare the 7 CRMs ↓</a><a class="lp-text-link" href="#trial-checklist">Use the free trial checklist →</a></div><p class="crm-brands">Close · HubSpot · Pipedrive · Freshsales · Zoho · Salesforce · monday CRM</p></div>
      <aside class="lp-brief" aria-labelledby="crm-brief-title"><p class="lp-kicker">During your CRM trial</p><h2 id="crm-brief-title">Check calls, callbacks<br>and handoffs.</h2><p class="crm-brief-intro">Start with the records your reps need on every call.</p><ol><li><span>01</span><div><strong>Contact details</strong><p>Keep the person's role, number and account together.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><strong>Call outcome</strong><p>Record whether they answered, requested a callback or booked a meeting.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><strong>Scheduled follow-up</strong><p>Assign the next task with an owner and due date.</p></div></li></ol><a href="#subscription-cost">See the subscription costs →</a></aside>
    </div>
    <p class="lp-direct-answer"><strong>Our starting shortlist:</strong> trial Close for calling inside the CRM, Pipedrive for pipeline visibility with a separate phone app, and Freshsales or Zoho when the subscription budget is tight. Give an existing HubSpot or Salesforce setup a fair chance before replacing it. Consider monday CRM for visual coordination and mobile calls.</p>
    <p class="lp-method"><strong>Sources checked {{ guide.reviewed }}.</strong> Official sources are linked in the reviews.</p>
  </div></div>
  <nav class="lp-jump" aria-label="On this page"><div class="lp-wrap"><a href="#comparison">Compare 7</a><a href="#subscription-cost">Simple costs</a><a href="#crm-reviews">Blunt verdicts</a><a href="#crm-matchups">Apollo &amp; comparisons</a><a href="#trial-checklist">Free trial checklist</a><a href="#questions">Questions</a></div></nav>

  <div class="lp-wrap"><p class="lp-note">Moving out of spreadsheets? Our <a href="/resources/best-crm-for-small-businesses/">best CRM for small businesses guide</a> covers first-CRM choices, small-team costs and a simple setup plan.</p></div>

  <section class="lp-section" id="comparison"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">01 / The short answer</p><h2>Which CRM fits<br>your sales team's day?</h2><p>Start with the calling setup your team needs. Compare the required plan, connected phone apps and additional fees.</p></div>
    <p class="lp-scroll-hint">Swipe the table to see the calling setup, limits and extra costs.</p>
    <div class="lp-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="crm-table-caption"><table class="lp-table crm-comparison"><caption id="crm-table-caption">Seven CRMs for cold calling and outbound sales: who they suit and what to check</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">CRM</th><th scope="col">Useful for</th><th scope="col">How calling fits</th><th scope="col">Limits and extra costs</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for p in guide.providers %}<tr><th scope="row"><a href="#{{ p.id }}">{{ p.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></th><td>{{ p.fit }}</td><td>{{ p.calling }}</td><td>{{ p.catch }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
    <div class="lp-note"><strong>Make follow-up easy to find.</strong><p>Assign an owner and due date to each follow-up, then check how easily reps can find those tasks.</p></div>
    <p class="lp-small">Considering a separate calling platform? <a href="/resources/nooks-alternatives/">Check Nooks alternatives before adding another subscription</a>.</p>
    <p class="lp-small">Already happy with your CRM? Compare <a href="/resources/best-cold-calling-dialers/">cold calling diallers that can work alongside it</a>. Still choosing the data? Start with our <a href="/resources/b2b-lead-providers/">B2B lead generation database comparison</a>.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="subscription-cost"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">02 / No budget form to fill in</p><h2>What does the<br>CRM subscription cost?</h2><p>Find your team size. These are <strong>USD monthly equivalents on annual billing</strong> for the named plans. Calling packages differ. Phone usage, required onboarding and other extras are listed separately.</p></div>
    <div class="lp-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="crm-cost-caption"><table class="lp-table crm-cost-table"><caption id="crm-cost-caption">Annual-plan CRM subscriptions for 1, 3 and 5 users. Not a complete calling bill.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">CRM and selected plan</th><th scope="col">1 user</th><th scope="col">3 users</th><th scope="col">5 users</th><th scope="col">Add this to the buying decision</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for p in guide.providers %}<tr data-cost-provider="{{ p.id }}"><th scope="row"><a href="#{{ p.id }}">{{ p.name }}</a><span class="crm-plan">{{ p.plan }}</span></th>{% for count in [1,3,5] %}{% set paidSeats = count %}{% if p.minSeats > count %}{% set paidSeats = p.minSeats %}{% endif %}<td data-user-count="{{ count }}">{% if p.annualRate %}<strong>USD {{ p.annualRate * paidSeats }}</strong><span class="crm-cost-unit">/ month{% if paidSeats > count %}<br>{{ paidSeats }} paid seats{% endif %}</span>{% else %}<strong class="crm-quote">Confirm setup</strong>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}<td>{{ p.costNote }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
    <p class="lp-small">Multiply a displayed monthly equivalent by 12 for the annual subscription. Taxes, currency conversion, phone usage and unlisted add-ons are excluded. monday sells seat buckets: one user needs three paid seats; four users need five. Salesforce Starter begins at USD 25/user/month, but we have not priced it as a complete calling-and-cadence setup. Each review links to the source and monthly-payment terms.</p>
    <div class="crm-cost-example"><span>Annual subscription examples</span><p><strong>Three Close Growth users:</strong> USD 297 monthly equivalent × 12 = <strong>USD 3,564/year</strong> for the CRM subscription. Add calling, numbers and any optional usage you buy.</p><p><strong>Three HubSpot Professional seats:</strong> USD 270 × 12 + USD 1,500 required onboarding = <strong>USD 4,740 in year one</strong>, before tax and other extras.</p></div>
    <div class="gr-budget"><h3>Budgeting for the campaign as well?</h3><p>Software is one expense. Use your calling costs, expected held meetings and customer economics to check the wider plan.</p><a href="/b2b-lead-generation-roi-calculator/">Calculate your campaign ROI →</a></div>
    <div class="crm-mid-cta"><div><h3>Get help with your outbound calls.</h3><p>CallTeam can research the accounts, make the calls and handle follow-up. Bring your current setup and tell us where the work is getting stuck.</p></div><a class="lp-button" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-booking-placement="crm-cost-cta">Book a free call ↗</a></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section" id="crm-reviews"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">03 / CallTeam's verdicts</p><h2>Our verdict on each CRM.</h2><p>Each review covers calling features, setup requirements and extra costs.</p></div>
    <nav class="lp-provider-nav" aria-label="CRM reviews">{% for p in guide.providers %}<a href="#{{ p.id }}">{{ p.name }}</a>{% endfor %}</nav>
    {% for p in guide.providers %}<article class="lp-provider" id="{{ p.id }}"><header class="lp-provider-head"><div><p class="lp-kicker">{{ p.tag }}</p><h3>{{ p.name }}</h3></div><a class="lp-source" href="{{ p.sources[0].url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official plans ↗</a></header><p class="crm-price-strip"><strong>{{ p.plan }}:</strong> {{ p.price }}</p><div class="lp-provider-body"><div class="lp-provider-detail"><h4>What it does well</h4><p>{{ p.strength }}</p><h4>What we do not like</h4><p>{{ p.drawback }}</p></div><aside class="lp-verdict"><p class="lp-kicker">The CallTeam verdict</p><p class="lp-verdict-text">{{ p.verdict }}</p><div><strong>Before you pay</strong><p>{{ p.check }}</p></div></aside></div><p class="lp-sources"><strong>Official sources:</strong> {% for source in p.sources %}<a href="{{ source.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ source.label }} ↗</a>{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>{% if p.id == "hubspot" %}<p class="lp-small">Facing a HubSpot upgrade or renewal? Compare <a href="/resources/hubspot-alternatives/">HubSpot CRM alternatives, first-year costs and switching checks</a>.</p>{% endif %}</article>{% endfor %}
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-paper" id="crm-matchups"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">04 / The comparisons buyers ask for</p><h2>Compare the CRMs<br>on your shortlist.</h2></div>
    <div class="lp-matchups crm-matchups"><div><h3>Close vs HubSpot</h3><p>Trial Close when the daily job centres on calls and follow-up. Give HubSpot serious weight when sales shares the wider customer record with marketing and other teams. Compare the relevant paid tiers, usage and onboarding. If your HubSpot workflow already works, a cheaper-looking seat elsewhere may not justify moving.</p></div><div><h3>Close vs Pipedrive</h3><p>Close Growth includes the power dialler. Pipedrive Growth gives you a pipeline and follow-up sequences, with a separate calling app for web calls. Compare the complete route from call to note to callback. Pick the combination that leaves fewer manual steps in your actual process.</p></div><div><h3>HubSpot vs Salesforce</h3><p>Start with the records and reporting the wider business needs. Then ask each vendor to demonstrate your calling and follow-up workflow on the quoted edition. An established company setup can be worth keeping. A small team should be equally willing to decide that the required configuration is more than it needs.</p></div><div><h3>Pipedrive vs monday CRM</h3><p>Compare the follow-up workflow behind the visual pipeline. Pipedrive's web calling comes through a connected app. monday offers native mobile calling, but its current Smart Call release lacks browser power dialling. Check the calling route and paid-seat minimum before choosing either by the look of its boards.</p></div></div>
    <div class="crm-apollo" id="apollo-and-crm"><p class="lp-kicker">Apollo deals, tasks and reporting</p><h3>Can Apollo replace a CRM?</h3><p>Apollo supports deals, tasks and pipeline reporting alongside prospecting and outreach. Check whether your existing plan covers the work your team needs to do.</p><p>Use the trial checklist to test ownership, callbacks, history, follow-up and opportunity reporting. If you connect HubSpot or Salesforce, confirm which system controls deal stages and how field updates sync.</p><p class="lp-sources"><strong>Official sources:</strong> <a href="https://knowledge.apollo.io/hc/en-us/articles/4415062467725-Deals-Overview" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apollo deals overview ↗</a> · <a href="https://knowledge.apollo.io/hc/en-us/articles/40691781463437-Set-Up-Deals" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pipeline and CRM sync rules ↗</a></p><a class="lp-text-link" href="/resources/b2b-lead-providers/#apollo">Read our Apollo data-provider verdict →</a><p class="lp-small">If contact coverage is the issue, compare <a href="/resources/apollo-alternatives/">Apollo alternatives and enrichment options</a> before changing the CRM.</p><p class="lp-small">Running LinkedIn sequences as well? Our <a href="/resources/best-linkedin-automation-tools/">LinkedIn automation comparison</a> covers reply handling, exports and the handoff your CRM needs.</p></div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-dark" id="trial-checklist"><div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-heading"><p class="lp-kicker">05 / Free. No email required.</p><h2>Six checks before<br>you commit to a CRM.</h2><p>Choose a CRM and run the six tasks during its demo or free trial. Tick each task after testing it, then record what worked, what failed and what needs checking.</p></div>
    <div class="crm-trial" data-crm-trial>
      <div class="crm-trial-top"><div><label for="crm-trial-vendor">Which CRM are you checking?</label><select id="crm-trial-vendor">{% for p in guide.providers %}<option value="{{ p.id }}">{{ p.name }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></div><div class="crm-trial-progress"><strong id="crm-trial-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">0 of 6 checks tried</strong><span id="crm-storage-note">Copy your checklist to keep the findings.</span></div></div>
      <ol class="crm-checks">{% for check in guide.checks %}<li><label for="crm-check-{{ check.id }}"><input id="crm-check-{{ check.id }}" type="checkbox" data-crm-check="{{ loop.index0 }}" disabled><span><strong>{{ check.title }}</strong><span>{{ check.text }}</span></span></label></li>{% endfor %}</ol>
      <div class="crm-trial-actions"><button class="lp-button crm-js-only" hidden type="button" id="crm-copy-checklist">Copy my checklist</button><a class="crm-download" href="/assets/downloads/outbound-crm-trial-checklist.txt" download="CallTeam-CRM-Trial-Checklist.txt">Download a blank checklist ↓</a><button type="button" class="crm-reset crm-js-only" id="crm-reset-checklist" hidden>Reset this CRM's checks</button></div><p id="crm-copy-status" class="crm-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <p class="lp-small">Use test records and numbers you control. Your progress is saved separately for each CRM in this browser when storage is available.</p>
      <noscript><p class="lp-small">Download the checklist or use the six checks above. Saving ticks and copying need JavaScript.</p></noscript>
    </div>
    <div class="crm-field-kit"><div><p class="lp-kicker">Follow-up fields to use</p><h3>Give every follow-up an owner.</h3><p>Keep mobile, direct and company numbers in separate fields. Give scheduled callbacks their own queue. Record an unanswered attempt against that number and schedule the next contact.</p><a class="crm-download" href="/resources/how-to-buy-cold-calling-leads/#calling-template">Get the calling-list template →</a></div><div><pre id="crm-fields-copy">Company and contact
Number type: mobile / direct / company
Last call outcome
Next action
Due date, time and prospect's time zone
Owner
Stop / suppression status</pre><button type="button" class="crm-reset crm-js-only" id="crm-copy-fields" hidden>Copy these follow-up fields</button><p id="crm-fields-status" class="crm-status" role="status"></p></div></div>
    <div class="gr-resources" aria-labelledby="crm-script-resources"><h3 id="crm-script-resources">Prepare your cold calling script.</h3><p>When you move from testing the workflow to making calls, bring an opening and questions that fit your buyer.</p>{% include "components/free-calling-resources.njk" %}</div>
  </div></section>

